   },
   "evidence": "At HEAD, assertDeliveryHead passes `current === head && !pending ? \"HEAD\" : current` to validateMerge. A completed pending merge therefore receives its literal SHA, bypassing `if (commit === \"HEAD\" && (await mergeHead(cwd))) throw new Error(\"Completed merge still has MERGE_HEAD\")`. prepareMerge subsequently validates the live HEAD and throws that generic Error. The failure handler excludes `DeliveryHeadError` from verified-draft publication, but this generic error reaches deliverVerifiedDraft, which pushes the verified SHA and creates a draft. At base, assertDeliveryHead called validateMerge without a commit argument; its unconditional MERGE_HEAD check failed inside the guard and became a DeliveryHeadError, suppressing publication."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A delivery merge gets committed, but the run is killed before git removes its 'merge in progress' marker. At base the factory refused that state outright and published nothing. At head the delivery guard accepts it, the merge step then fails with a generic error, and the failure handler pushes the reviewed commit to GitHub and opens a '[needs human]' draft PR that the guard used to prevent.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "Throwaway test written under $TMPDIR, adapted from the interruptGatedMerge harness in test/pipeline-delivery-restart.test.ts. The base advances during review, a kill fault is set on the 2nd 'stage:gates:before' so the clean merge M=[R,F1] is committed and pendingRebaseSha=F1 with preRebaseHead=R. MERGE_HEAD=F1 is then written into the worktree's git dir and the run is resumed. Run with `bun test $TMPDIR/f1repro.*/f1.test.ts -t 'single advance'` at head, and the same file against a `git archive 9396b05` copy for base.",
    "output": "HEAD:  STATE pending= true preRebaseHead=reviewed true / RESULT1 status= needs_human error= Completed merge still has MERGE_HEAD prUrl= https://github.com/test/repo/pull/1 / RESULT1 refs changed= true pr create= true\nBASE:  STATE pending= true preRebaseHead=reviewed true / RESULT1 status= needs_human error= Delivery refused: expected checked SHA ace7daae..., actual HEAD 68c7970f... prUrl= null / RESULT1 refs changed= false pr create= false"
   },
   "evidence": "Head engine.ts:1978-1983 passes `current === head && !pending ? \"HEAD\" : current` to validateMerge. When pendingRebaseSha is set, the current HEAD is validated by SHA. merge.ts:39 at head only checks MERGE_HEAD when `commit === \"HEAD\"`, so a committed pending merge that still has MERGE_HEAD passes the guard. Base used `validateMerge(worktree, expected, base)` on HEAD, which threw 'Completed merge still has MERGE_HEAD', and that was turned into a DeliveryHeadError. Next, mergeForDelivery \u2192 prepareMerge (HEAD != before) \u2192 validateMerge(cwd, R, F1, 'HEAD') throws a plain Error. engine.ts:346-360 then takes the verifiedFailure branch because the error is not a DeliveryHeadError, and deliverVerifiedDraft pushes lastVerifiedSha and creates a draft PR. Severity is minor: git removes MERGE_HEAD as part of the commit, so this state needs a crash in a very small window or outside tampering. The draft also carries the reviewed, verified commit R, not the unchecked merge."
  }
